{"id": "mid-market-urban-alchemy", "title": "Street-ambassador money ran through a no-staff foundation to one contractor", "seconds": 130.3, "voice": "elevenlabs:OUMCzFUTd0F4Q6lkLkco", "narrator": "Roxy", "tempo": 1.147, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "2457cd0095db45a5", "words": 394, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "sfmap", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "San Francisco pays for street ambassadors on Mid-Market and Tenderloin streets.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.25, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "sfmap", "hood": "Tenderloin", "zoom": "hood", "scale": 2.6, "kicker": "Mid-Market and the Tenderloin"}, "emph": ["street ambassadors"], "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.78, 1.07, 1.25, 1.55, 2.17, 2.31, 2.83, 2.94, 3.49]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[0]", "established[6]"], "text": "But it didn’t hire the ambassador company.", "t0": 4.37, "t1": 6.25, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "Office of Economic and Workforce Development", "sub": "the grant maker"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Mid-Market Foundation", "sub": "no employees"}, {"art": "van", "name": "Urban Alchemy", "sub": "the ambassadors"}], "kicker": "Where the money went"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.21, 0.49, 0.75, 0.85, 1.4]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[0]", "established[6]"], "text": "It paid a foundation with no employees. The foundation paid Urban Alchemy.", "t0": 6.37, "t1": 10.73, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "Office of Economic and Workforce Development", "sub": "the grant maker"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Mid-Market Foundation", "sub": "no employees"}, {"art": "van", "name": "Urban Alchemy", "sub": "the ambassadors"}], "kicker": "Where the money went"}, "emph": ["no employees"], "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.35, 0.42, 0.93, 1.11, 1.26, 2.4, 2.56, 3.09, 3.46, 3.84]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["links[0]", "oneLine"], "text": "About 82 million dollars went through it.", "t0": 10.85, "t1": 13.04, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$82,436,756", "label": "paid to Mid-Market Foundation, fiscal 2022 to 2027"}, "emph": ["About"], "wt": [0.0, 0.31, 0.77, 1.1, 1.46, 1.67, 1.95]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[2]", "sources"], "text": "In 2025, the Board’s Budget and Legislative Analyst reviewed it. These are official findings.", "t0": 13.56, "t1": 19.05, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Official findings", "sub": "Budget and Legislative Analyst, February 2025"}, "emph": ["official findings"], "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.42, 1.06, 1.16, 1.51, 1.89, 2.0, 2.55, 3.0, 3.39, 4.04, 4.31, 4.45, 4.85]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "The grant began in July 2022 at 9 million dollars.", "t0": 19.27, "t1": 22.41, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["July 1, 2022, approved by OEWD alone", "$9,000,000"], "b": ["the level that needs a Board vote", "$10 million"], "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.37, 0.66, 0.74, 1.09, 1.4, 1.87, 2.01, 2.26, 2.6]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "That’s under 10 million, the level that needs a Board vote.", "t0": 22.53, "t1": 24.97, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["July 1, 2022, approved by OEWD alone", "$9,000,000"], "b": ["the level that needs a Board vote", "$10 million"], "arrows": false}, "emph": ["under 10 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.43, 0.66, 1.01, 1.11, 1.36, 1.48, 1.72, 1.78, 2.06]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[1]"], "text": "Then the Board approved increase after increase. Today the ceiling is 68.85 million.", "t0": 25.09, "t1": 30.59, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "The grant’s ceiling, contract 1000026131", "rows": [["Today", "68851756"], ["July 2023", "60590570"], ["March 2023", "33590570"], ["November 2022", "20490000"], ["July 2022", "9000000"]]}, "emph": ["68.85 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.24, 0.48, 0.91, 1.42, 1.71, 2.64, 3.06, 3.16, 3.49, 3.59, 4.18, 4.46, 4.69, 5.01]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]"], "text": "In November 2023, the department added money on its own. How much?", "t0": 30.81, "t1": 35.18, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Amendment 4", "kicker": "November 1, 2023", "sub": "approved by OEWD alone"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.55, 0.82, 1.35, 1.45, 1.93, 2.2, 2.47, 2.6, 2.78, 3.64, 3.88]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "established[0]"], "text": "Exactly 500,000 dollars.", "t0": 35.18, "t1": 37.35, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$500,000", "label": "added with no Board vote"}, "emph": ["Exactly"], "wt": [0.04, 0.58, 0.89, 1.2, 1.6]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "suspicious[1].why", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "The Charter needs a vote for anything more.", "t0": 37.87, "t1": 39.73, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Board approval for a modification of “more than $500,000”"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.47, 0.7, 0.77, 1.03, 1.17, 1.52]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "suspicious[1].why", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "So that’s the most it could add without one. The record doesn’t give the reason.", "t0": 39.85, "t1": 43.34, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Board approval for a modification of “more than $500,000”"}, "emph": ["without one"], "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.44, 0.55, 0.78, 0.86, 1.01, 1.24, 1.6, 1.98, 2.16, 2.44, 2.72, 2.93, 3.04]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[2]"], "text": "Then the foundation asked for advances.", "t0": 43.56, "t1": 46.16, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["advance asked, November 2024", "$2.5 million"], "b": ["advance asked, January 2025", "$3 million"], "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.27, 0.82, 1.11, 1.27]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[2]"], "text": "2.5 million dollars, then 3 million. What for?", "t0": 46.16, "t1": 50.45, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["advance asked, November 2024", "$2.5 million"], "b": ["advance asked, January 2025", "$3 million"], "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.04, 0.28, 0.55, 0.82, 1.1, 1.48, 1.67, 1.93, 2.89, 3.17]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "suspicious[2].why", "established[3]"], "text": "So Urban Alchemy could make payroll. Public money, ahead of schedule, to cover a contractor’s cash shortfall.", "t0": 50.45, "t1": 56.63, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "to ensure that Urban Alchemy had adequate cash flow to make payroll"}, "emph": ["make payroll"], "wt": [0.04, 0.3, 0.64, 1.03, 1.17, 1.36, 2.46, 2.88, 3.25, 3.54, 3.62, 4.07, 4.18, 4.44, 4.52, 5.18, 5.55]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["innocent[2]"], "text": "Urban Alchemy says the City often pays late.", "t0": 56.75, "t1": 58.97, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "van", "label": "Urban Alchemy", "kicker": "Its side", "sub": "says the City regularly pays late"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.31, 0.66, 0.89, 1.0, 1.27, 1.56, 1.86]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "suspicious[3].why", "established[4]"], "text": "Meanwhile, required reports were overdue. They’re the City’s proof the work was done.", "t0": 59.09, "t1": 63.44, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "doc", "kicker": "Overdue, February 2025", "source": "s5", "text": "Not submitted: the December 2024 activity report; quarterly and semi-annual reports due December 2024 and January 2025; reports on the Ellis Street and Willow Alley expansions.", "mark": "Not submitted"}, "emph": ["overdue"], "wt": [0.0, 0.52, 0.96, 1.39, 1.59, 2.52, 2.75, 2.86, 3.19, 3.51, 3.62, 3.85, 4.0]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["links[4]"], "text": "The foundation was run by a consulting firm, Urban Place Consulting Group.", "t0": 63.66, "t1": 67.42, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Urban Place Consulting Group", "kicker": "Paid to run the foundation", "sub": "management services, 2024", "chip": "$811,970"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.68, 0.84, 1.06, 1.2, 1.27, 1.83, 2.21, 2.55, 2.86, 3.44]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["links[4]"], "text": "811,970 dollars in 2024.", "t0": 67.54, "t1": 71.26, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Urban Place Consulting Group", "kicker": "Paid to run the foundation", "sub": "management services, 2024", "chip": "$811,970"}, "emph": ["811,970"], "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.56, 0.89, 1.33, 1.56, 1.87, 2.21, 2.57, 2.67, 3.0]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[5]", "oneLine"], "text": "Contracting directly, the analyst said, would save at least 850,400 dollars a year.", "t0": 71.38, "t1": 77.02, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$850,400", "label": "a year, at least", "sub": "saved by contracting directly, the analyst estimated"}, "emph": ["850,400"], "wt": [0.0, 0.55, 0.99, 1.11, 1.51, 2.1, 2.3, 2.51, 2.62, 2.92, 3.18, 3.52, 3.83, 4.29, 4.55, 4.83, 5.2, 5.29]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "suspicious[4].what", "notEstablished[3]"], "text": "The tax returns also report a property rental with the board’s vice chair.", "t0": 77.14, "t1": 80.83, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "The board vice chair", "kicker": "Board vice chair", "sub": "“rental of property,” 2022 to 2024; the returns do not say who is landlord", "chip": "$140,500"}, "emph": ["vice chair"], "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.46, 0.94, 1.3, 1.63, 1.7, 2.12, 2.47, 2.61, 2.7, 3.02, 3.3]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "suspicious[4].what", "notEstablished[3]"], "text": "140,500 dollars over three years.", "t0": 80.95, "t1": 84.31, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "The board vice chair", "kicker": "Board vice chair", "sub": "“rental of property,” 2022 to 2024; the returns do not say who is landlord", "chip": "$140,500"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.24, 0.56, 0.85, 1.34, 1.61, 1.86, 2.33, 2.59, 2.88]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[13]"], "text": "Yet its reports to the Attorney General answered no to any director deal, three years running.", "t0": 84.43, "t1": 89.01, "shot": "b15a", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "'No' to any lease or other transaction with a director: 2022, 2023 and 2024"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.36, 0.8, 0.92, 1.02, 1.43, 1.82, 2.24, 2.49, 2.63, 2.85, 3.31, 3.59, 3.85, 4.14]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[8]", "established[10]"], "text": "The Controller’s monitors flagged it too.", "t0": 89.23, "t1": 91.21, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Tier 2", "kicker": "The Controller’s monitors", "sub": "8 standards unmet in FY2024, 9 in FY2025"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.62, 1.1, 1.48, 1.6]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[8]", "established[10]"], "text": "It failed nine standards, and went on their Tier 2 list.", "t0": 91.33, "t1": 94.06, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Tier 2", "kicker": "The Controller’s monitors", "sub": "8 standards unmet in FY2024, 9 in FY2025"}, "emph": ["Tier 2"], "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.49, 0.77, 1.35, 1.45, 1.61, 1.69, 1.85, 2.1, 2.32]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[11]"], "text": "Its 2020 report to the charity registry showed revenue of 7,500 dollars.", "t0": 94.18, "t1": 99.18, "shot": "b16a", "visual": {"type": "versus", "kicker": "Mid Market Foundation", "a": ["gross revenue, 2020", "$7,500.00"], "b": ["City paid, fiscal 2022", "$12,165,000.00"]}, "emph": ["7,500"], "wt": [0.0, 0.24, 0.55, 0.85, 1.23, 1.32, 1.4, 1.79, 2.27, 2.56, 2.93, 3.03, 3.36, 3.81, 4.1, 4.42]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[11]", "established[12]"], "text": "In fiscal 2022, on two earlier grants, the City paid it 12.17 million.", "t0": 99.3, "t1": 104.18, "shot": "b16a", "visual": {"type": "versus", "kicker": "Mid Market Foundation", "a": ["gross revenue, 2020", "$7,500.00"], "b": ["City paid, fiscal 2022", "$12,165,000.00"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.49, 0.75, 1.38, 1.55, 1.78, 2.15, 2.5, 2.61, 2.88, 3.11, 3.19, 3.54, 3.81, 4.04, 4.38]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[11]", "established[12]"], "text": "The registry now lists it past due.", "t0": 104.3, "t1": 106.13, "shot": "b16a", "visual": {"type": "versus", "kicker": "Mid Market Foundation", "a": ["gross revenue, 2020", "$7,500.00"], "b": ["City paid, fiscal 2022", "$12,165,000.00"]}, "emph": ["past due"], "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.55, 0.77, 1.03, 1.15, 1.49]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[9]", "story[4]"], "text": "Then the money moved. The foundation’s City payments fell to 3.5 million.", "t0": 106.25, "t1": 110.97, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["City payments to the foundation, FY2025", "$26.04M"], "b": ["FY2026", "$3.50M"]}, "emph": ["3.5 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.25, 0.5, 1.49, 1.67, 2.31, 2.61, 3.07, 3.3, 3.39, 3.63, 3.9, 4.23]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[9]", "story[4]"], "text": "Urban Alchemy is now paid directly.", "t0": 111.09, "t1": 112.84, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["City payments to the foundation, FY2025", "$26.04M"], "b": ["FY2026", "$3.50M"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.31, 0.63, 0.74, 0.95, 1.2]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "No authority has found money missing. The records don’t show whether the late reports came in.", "t0": 113.06, "t1": 117.85, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That ambassadors did not work, or money went missing", "Whether the reports came in and the advances were reconciled"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.66, 0.79, 1.03, 1.28, 2.14, 2.33, 2.7, 2.97, 3.23, 3.49, 3.59, 3.81, 4.25, 4.53]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[2]"], "text": "What would settle it? The department’s grant file, and the vice chair’s lease.", "t0": 117.97, "t1": 121.99, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "OEWD’s grant file: the overdue reports and the advances"}, {"who": "", "what": "The lease behind the vice chair’s rent"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.28, 0.59, 1.3, 1.47, 1.99, 2.29, 2.7, 2.84, 2.92, 3.19, 3.57]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status"], "text": "The pass-through has largely ended. The foundation is on the Controller’s Tier 2 list.", "t0": 122.11, "t1": 127.03, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.78, 0.99, 1.46, 2.27, 2.43, 3.02, 3.15, 3.25, 3.33, 3.88, 4.2, 4.48]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 127.15, "t1": 129.43, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.36, 0.7, 0.84, 1.13, 1.21, 1.29, 1.55, 1.84]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The finding", "lead1": "Under the line", "lead2": "Exactly $500,000", "lead3": "Cash for payroll", "lead4": "The middle layer", "lead5": "Tier 2", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "flow", "hook": "person"}